WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:01.850
Miss Cecilia!

00:04.320 --> 00:05.980
Lawren?!

00:07.420 --> 00:09.740
You are even more 
overprotective than I've heard.

00:10.420 --> 00:12.980
I am Giselbert Aldridge.

00:12.980 --> 00:17.740
It seems my little sister, Hazelita, 
has imposed on you quite a bit.

00:18.580 --> 00:21.170
You're Miss Hazelita's older brother?

00:21.170 --> 00:23.740
Has Hazelita told you about me?

00:23.740 --> 00:26.370
If I had to say one or the other, 
it was Abel who told us.

00:26.380 --> 00:28.370
Well, that's a sad thing.

00:28.710 --> 00:32.330
By the way, the lady 
there seems to have melted.

00:34.880 --> 00:38.260
Sai— Um... what's wrong?

00:38.690 --> 00:40.050
My name.

00:40.050 --> 00:42.260
You called me by my
name just then, and yet...

00:46.240 --> 00:49.950
It seems the pastor and 
the lady saint are on very good terms.

00:49.950 --> 00:54.450
May I ask that you keep the fact that 
she is a lady saint as secret as possible?

00:55.500 --> 00:57.200
If that's how things stand...

00:57.200 --> 00:59.750
then let's continue our 
conversation at the mansion.

02:32.250 --> 02:36.010
Episode 8

02:32.250 --> 02:36.010
Frederica's Bequest

02:36.460 --> 02:39.000
You took Cecilia's hand?

02:39.000 --> 02:40.510
Of all the things to do.

02:40.510 --> 02:42.260
You're unbelievable, Brother.

02:42.260 --> 02:46.180
A foolish action like that... 
It's no wonder Lawrence was wary of you.

02:46.180 --> 02:48.930
You're both being very harsh.

02:48.930 --> 02:51.940
Hazelita, we haven't seen 
each other in so long.

02:51.940 --> 02:54.060
It's all right to be sweet to me!

02:55.020 --> 02:57.190
Oh. You have the same color hair, don't you?

02:57.190 --> 02:58.150
Indeed we do!

02:58.150 --> 03:02.950
We siblings have inherited 
this hair color from our mother!

03:02.950 --> 03:04.690
Matching one's little sister...

03:04.690 --> 03:06.630
It's just wonderful, don't you think?

03:05.580 --> 03:08.500
I suppose I'll introduce you properly.

03:08.500 --> 03:13.460
This is my older brother, 
and the person who hired Abel, Giselbert.

03:13.460 --> 03:15.570
Our parents are on an official trip, 
so they aren't here.

03:15.570 --> 03:17.590
He's the master of this 
place in their stead.

03:17.590 --> 03:19.590
Is this what they call a sister compl—

03:19.590 --> 03:22.460
As a formal introduction, 
my name is Lawrence.

03:22.460 --> 03:25.680
I take care of the lady saint's every need.

03:25.680 --> 03:31.540
So, every interaction with 
the lady saint must go through me first.

03:31.540 --> 03:32.570
What's this?

03:32.570 --> 03:34.520
Now, please don't be so on your guard.

03:34.520 --> 03:37.400
My little sister hasn't 
ever brought friends over.

03:37.400 --> 03:38.560
It makes me so happy.

03:38.810 --> 03:41.200
Please relax here for the next few days.

03:41.200 --> 03:43.280
You are very welcome.

03:46.340 --> 03:49.040
For now, shall we have dinner?

03:49.040 --> 03:50.280
How extravagant!

03:50.280 --> 03:53.300
He just makes a big deal 
of everything, that's all.

03:54.390 --> 03:57.520
Phew, I ate so much.

03:57.520 --> 03:58.400
Abel!

03:58.400 --> 03:59.180
Huh?

03:59.180 --> 04:02.930
Hazelita seems to have completely 
opened up to the two of them.

04:02.930 --> 04:04.770
Yes, she has.

04:04.770 --> 04:08.120
She tries to protect
Saint Cecilia in her own way.

04:08.120 --> 04:10.350
Though she does fail 
in her attempts sometimes.

04:10.350 --> 04:14.040
When I think back to 
when she was stuck in her shell...

04:14.040 --> 04:17.240
Asking you to be her tutor was 
the right thing to do, don't you think?

04:17.240 --> 04:19.480
Though, she does need 
a lot of looking after.

04:19.480 --> 04:22.240
Let's just say that's part of the job.

04:22.240 --> 04:25.000
Then please give me a raise.

04:25.610 --> 04:27.080
I'll think about it.

04:28.420 --> 04:30.310
Hey there, Lawrence!

04:30.740 --> 04:33.240
Are you the type to drink alcohol?

04:33.240 --> 04:35.510
Y-Yes, technically.

04:37.360 --> 04:41.970
I invited Abel, too, but he's always 
so stubborn, refusing to drink.

04:41.970 --> 04:42.870
Oh, yes.

04:42.870 --> 04:45.730
I've never seen him drink either.

04:45.730 --> 04:48.340
He's just fundamentally 
too free in his actions.

04:48.340 --> 04:50.410
Given that, it's amazing 
that you paired him

04:50.410 --> 04:52.480
with Hazelita, who seems 
to stick to the rules.

04:52.480 --> 04:56.320
There is a part of her that's 
supported by Abel, though.

04:56.550 --> 05:00.420
She is forceful and can be inflexible.

05:00.420 --> 05:02.480
Though, I think that part of her is cute.

05:02.790 --> 05:07.780
In contrast, she was very earnest 
when she was little, and that was cute, too.

05:08.040 --> 05:10.330
You seem to be very proud of her.

05:10.330 --> 05:13.920
Being so loved, Hazelita must be very happy.

05:13.920 --> 05:14.950
What's this?

05:15.360 --> 05:19.710
There are times when you want to brag 
about the lady saint, aren't there?

05:19.710 --> 05:21.300
About the lady saint?

05:21.560 --> 05:23.870
She's good enough to get 
Hazelita's seal of approval.

05:23.870 --> 05:26.840
I'm sure she must be important to you, too.

05:27.060 --> 05:29.960
Make sure you don't lose her.

05:30.350 --> 05:31.020
Gi—

05:31.020 --> 05:32.330
Lawren!

05:33.140 --> 05:34.730
So this is where you've been.

05:34.730 --> 05:36.100
Lady Saint!

05:36.100 --> 05:38.850
You've been with Mister Giselbert?

05:39.880 --> 05:41.860
What are you drinking?

05:41.860 --> 05:43.280
It's alcohol.

05:43.280 --> 05:44.940
I'm only having a little, though.

05:44.940 --> 05:46.700
Miss Cecilia, will you be drinking, too?

05:46.700 --> 05:47.940
She will not!

05:49.240 --> 05:51.080
The next day.

05:51.900 --> 05:54.320
To think they'd tell 
the two of us to go on ahead.

05:54.320 --> 05:56.710
It feels like this is different 
than we'd discussed somehow.

05:56.710 --> 05:58.770
Abel isn't waking up!

05:58.770 --> 06:02.990
Lawrence, will you 
and Cecilia go on ahead, please?

06:03.850 --> 06:06.840
<i>And it seemed like Eric 
wanted to say something.</i>

06:08.840 --> 06:12.600
For now, shall we look around 
the city, just the two of us?

06:13.840 --> 06:14.920
Yes!

06:39.620 --> 06:41.620
They have so many different kinds of things!

06:41.620 --> 06:44.130
These are accessories with flower motifs.

06:44.430 --> 06:46.380
What do you think of this?

06:46.380 --> 06:48.080
It's modeled after a poppy.

06:49.080 --> 06:51.640
It's so lovely!

06:53.380 --> 06:54.830
Shall we buy it?

06:54.830 --> 06:55.600
What?

06:55.600 --> 06:57.580
You have a big appetite for food,

06:57.580 --> 07:00.040
but you don't crave material things 
very often, so every once in a while...

07:01.470 --> 07:04.240
Since you're buying it, 
why don't you put it on?

07:04.510 --> 07:05.450
Here you go.

07:05.970 --> 07:09.120
Huh? Why did you give it to me?

07:09.120 --> 07:10.940
If it's a gift,

07:10.940 --> 07:13.270
then I thought that putting it 
on for her should be part of the package.

07:14.280 --> 07:15.750
I see.

07:15.750 --> 07:17.110
Lawren.

07:18.880 --> 07:21.000
Will you be able to put it on me?

07:27.500 --> 07:30.500
You're amazing, Lawren! 
Your fingers are so nimble!

07:30.810 --> 07:33.110
Come on, let's go.

07:35.400 --> 07:37.100
I'll treasure it.

07:39.140 --> 07:41.990
Coming here to this city with you

07:42.100 --> 07:45.490
and you calling my name 
for the first time will make great memories!

07:48.040 --> 07:50.370
There's no need to remember that, is there?

07:50.370 --> 07:51.780
Yes, there is!

07:51.780 --> 07:56.160
It's only because you don't 
usually call me by name, you know?

07:57.500 --> 08:00.960
I'll work hard so that one day it will be 
natural for me to call you by name.

08:02.160 --> 08:04.000
It's going to be afternoon soon.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.280
Oh, Lawrence! You silly!

08:04.000 --> 08:06.170
Let's look for everyone else 
and have some lunch!

08:06.390 --> 08:07.970
All right!

08:09.130 --> 08:11.890
<i>Her name, huh?</i>

08:15.180 --> 08:18.260
<i>This is another very impressive garden.</i>

08:18.500 --> 08:21.520
<i>Now that I think about it, 
this side of the city...</i>

08:21.520 --> 08:23.780
<i>I've never been here before, have I?</i>

08:32.440 --> 08:35.180
Why did you want to go 
out of your way to eat this?

08:35.180 --> 08:36.700
Because it's unusual!

08:36.700 --> 08:40.420
Lawren, is this something 
you bite directly into to eat?

08:40.420 --> 08:42.200
It wouldn't be unseemly of me?

08:42.200 --> 08:43.980
Why are you asking that now?

08:44.750 --> 08:46.210
It tastes of the city.

08:50.960 --> 08:52.460
The city!

08:52.460 --> 08:55.360
The city... The city...

08:55.370 --> 08:56.920
Now, Lawrence.

08:56.920 --> 08:59.220
What did you and Cecilia go see?

08:59.220 --> 09:00.040
What?

09:00.040 --> 09:03.310
Just what you'd expect, unusual things, 
accessories, things like that.

09:07.680 --> 09:09.860
Well, I suppose you get 
passing marks for that!

09:09.860 --> 09:12.940
Why do you seem so happy, Miss Hazelita?

09:12.940 --> 09:16.920
Lately, the lady's meddling 
has been increasing.

09:16.920 --> 09:19.080
I don't want to hear 
that from you of all people!

09:19.080 --> 09:20.620
I'm sorry!

09:20.620 --> 09:22.980
It's because the lady stood up so suddenly.

09:22.980 --> 09:24.710
I'll go borrow something to wipe it up with.

09:24.970 --> 09:27.020
I'll go with you!

09:28.870 --> 09:31.690
Lawren? Is something wrong?

09:31.690 --> 09:32.420
N-No.

09:32.420 --> 09:34.590
For some reason, my head hurts.

09:34.590 --> 09:35.730
What?

09:35.730 --> 09:36.960
I'm all right.

09:36.960 --> 09:39.360
It hasn't been as bad lately,

09:39.680 --> 09:42.480
but I've had this happen every once 
in a while since I was a child.

09:42.480 --> 09:43.780
Saint Cecilia,

09:43.780 --> 09:46.030
have you bestowed too much 
of your protection again?

09:46.030 --> 09:49.240
No. I've been careful since then.

09:49.240 --> 09:52.720
Lawren, how long have you felt this way?

09:52.720 --> 09:55.320
Um... Oh, right.

09:55.320 --> 09:57.930
Since we passed that garden.

09:58.900 --> 10:02.020
I think you should try decreasing 
the protection on Lawrence.

10:02.390 --> 10:03.490
All right!

10:08.750 --> 10:11.740
Oh. It's starting to fade.

10:12.450 --> 10:14.000
I'm so glad.

10:14.520 --> 10:18.260
Abel, what's in that garden?

10:18.480 --> 10:19.980
That garden...

10:20.230 --> 10:22.770
is a certain someone's 
resting place, you see.

10:23.180 --> 10:25.020
A certain someone?

10:25.270 --> 10:29.120
Someone who once lived in this town, 
Lady Saint Frederica.

10:38.400 --> 10:40.290
Lady Saint Frederica?

10:40.290 --> 10:41.300
Yes.

10:41.300 --> 10:45.540
You were probably affected by Lady 
Saint Frederica's divine protection.

10:45.540 --> 10:46.840
But that means...

10:46.840 --> 10:48.540
You can't possibly mean 
that in the garden...

10:48.540 --> 10:49.640
Abel.

10:51.790 --> 10:54.360
Are you sneaking around trying 
to do something in secret again?

10:54.360 --> 10:56.180
That's not what's going on here.

10:56.180 --> 10:59.300
Besides, you haven't really told 
them everything, have you, Miss?

11:00.800 --> 11:03.190
Since we have come back to this city,

11:03.190 --> 11:06.070
I had planned to tell them everything.

11:06.380 --> 11:08.300
About what I saw when I was little...

11:08.520 --> 11:10.340
about the lady saint.

11:11.190 --> 11:16.610
Saint Frederica was brought here by 
a wealthy family with influence in this city.

11:16.610 --> 11:19.080
As the daughter of a prominent family,

11:19.080 --> 11:22.820
I often went to see her 
as she relaxed in the garden.

11:24.190 --> 11:25.950
Hazelita!

11:25.950 --> 11:27.740
You've come to see me again today!

11:27.740 --> 11:30.080
I came to make a flower crown.

11:30.700 --> 11:33.730
Her long hair would flutter...

11:33.730 --> 11:36.980
and she wore red dresses. She was beautiful.

11:38.110 --> 11:40.350
Those stricken with illness, 
or those who were injured...

11:40.600 --> 11:44.180
when they spoke with the lady saint, 
their hearts would be set at ease.

11:44.180 --> 11:47.830
That reputation lead to her being called 
the Lady Saint of Compassion.

11:47.830 --> 11:52.900
And there were more than a few people who
would come just to gaze at her gentle smile.

11:53.600 --> 11:55.600
Now that I think of it, Lady Saint,

11:55.600 --> 11:57.750
my big brother said he would come later.

11:58.090 --> 12:01.420
What? School finishes 
early today, doesn't it?

12:01.420 --> 12:03.660
Do you think I should 
prepare something for him?

12:04.400 --> 12:06.180
That flower crown?

12:06.180 --> 12:08.040
Th-That's...

12:08.040 --> 12:10.750
I haven't made mine very well.

12:10.750 --> 12:13.610
You've made so many 
and you still haven't improved?

12:14.250 --> 12:15.290
Gil!

12:15.600 --> 12:18.360
Hazelita, have you been a good girl?

12:19.040 --> 12:19.880
Ow!

12:19.880 --> 12:20.980
Oh my.

12:20.980 --> 12:23.450
Hazelita is always a good girl.

12:23.450 --> 12:26.880
Unlike a certain someone, she never 
suddenly appears standing behind me.

12:26.880 --> 12:29.760
Isn't it partly your fault for not noticing?

12:29.760 --> 12:31.350
I can't help it.

12:31.350 --> 12:34.280
I was absorbed in our conversation.

12:34.280 --> 12:36.140
Even among all the people in the city,

12:36.140 --> 12:39.270
the ones who spent the most time with her...

12:39.270 --> 12:41.560
were us siblings.

12:41.960 --> 12:45.480
She was unreliable in some ways, 
but she was a warm person.

12:45.880 --> 12:48.040
She was a person who should 
have been loved, and yet...

12:49.260 --> 12:51.370
The wealthy family 
that kept control of her...

12:51.680 --> 12:56.260
worshiped her holiness
and didn't treat her as a person.

12:56.260 --> 12:57.880
And that wasn't all.

12:57.880 --> 13:00.380
The people in town 
were swept up in the same belief.

13:00.380 --> 13:03.010
Anyone who opposed was put under pressure.

13:03.010 --> 13:05.390
It was as though the city was enthralled.

13:05.830 --> 13:09.510
There wasn't anything I could do.

13:10.040 --> 13:13.890
And it seems it was the
same for my older brother.

13:13.890 --> 13:15.770
Newspaper articles 
from the time said that the

13:15.770 --> 13:18.400
Great Lady Saint was 
the one who calmed things.

13:18.670 --> 13:19.900
It's true.

13:19.900 --> 13:22.560
I don't know who it was from...

13:22.560 --> 13:24.490
but the Great Lady Saint 
received a secret report.

13:24.490 --> 13:27.780
A messenger from her arrived 
and the situation was brought under control.

13:28.100 --> 13:32.540
But by that point, the amount of time left 
to the lady saint was...

13:33.100 --> 13:34.600
I tended her deathbed.

13:34.880 --> 13:36.790
We did, as a family.

13:37.300 --> 13:40.190
<i>If she was someone 
important to Miss Hazelita,</i>

13:40.190 --> 13:42.610
<i>then Mister Giselbert, 
who was with her then, must also...</i>

13:43.040 --> 13:44.180
Um.

13:44.180 --> 13:48.190
Was this something 
that I was supposed to hear?

13:48.190 --> 13:50.820
I'm actually glad that you heard it.

13:51.140 --> 13:55.160
It's something that 
as many people as possible

13:55.160 --> 13:57.380
should hear so that it never happens again.

13:57.380 --> 14:02.120
I'm sorry for telling such a 
dark story in a place like this.

14:02.120 --> 14:03.280
Not at all.

14:03.280 --> 14:07.030
Thank you so much for telling us, Hazelita.

14:10.780 --> 14:15.340
I've never spoken to anyone 
about her this much before.

14:15.340 --> 14:17.450
Miss, I bet your palms are a sweaty mess.

14:17.450 --> 14:18.540
Shut up.

14:18.670 --> 14:21.920
Up until now, you hated 
speaking of it at all, and yet...

14:21.920 --> 14:26.000
Maybe something inside you 
has changed, miss?

14:28.030 --> 14:29.560
Yes, you're right.

14:32.430 --> 14:34.940
<i>Lady Saint Frederica's divine blessing.</i>

14:35.240 --> 14:38.820
<i>Is there something she's trying to tell me?</i>

14:41.480 --> 14:44.610
<i>I haven't seen Mister Giselbert today.</i>

14:45.480 --> 14:48.950
<b>Fidget Fidget</b>

14:46.160 --> 14:49.390
Um... This way? No, it was...

14:49.390 --> 14:50.760
Um...

14:49.720 --> 14:51.330
What are you doing?

14:51.700 --> 14:53.360
L-Lawren!

14:53.360 --> 14:56.740
After hearing Hazelita's story,

14:56.740 --> 14:58.870
I couldn't help wondering about the garden.

14:58.870 --> 14:59.410
What?

14:59.410 --> 15:02.210
You can't mean to go 
there this late at night?

15:02.720 --> 15:03.700
Oh.

15:03.960 --> 15:06.220
That's Mister Giselbert, isn't it?

15:06.220 --> 15:08.090
It's night. Where could he be going?

15:08.090 --> 15:10.350
He has a bouquet of flowers, doesn't he?

15:10.350 --> 15:11.600
You're right.

15:11.600 --> 15:15.100
Maybe he's going to see 
someone he's close with?

15:15.100 --> 15:16.560
Lady Saint?

15:21.220 --> 15:22.750
This is...

15:22.750 --> 15:24.980
It's the garden we were talking about.

15:27.760 --> 15:30.420
I'm impressed that you 
followed me without losing me.

15:30.420 --> 15:33.320
Um, I was the one who followed you.

15:33.320 --> 15:35.130
Lawren just came along with me.

15:35.130 --> 15:37.170
What are you saying?

15:37.170 --> 15:39.640
I'm just as bad as you for not stopping you!

15:39.640 --> 15:41.470
We're very sorry, Mister Giselbert.

15:41.470 --> 15:42.400
Lawren!

15:42.400 --> 15:45.220
Please don't apologize 
before I have the chance to!

15:45.220 --> 15:48.340
You wondered where I was going 
with a bouquet of flowers, right?

15:48.770 --> 15:51.300
Would you like to come meet 
the person I'm giving them to?

15:53.740 --> 15:57.900
This garden was once the property 
of a certain wealthy family.

15:57.900 --> 16:01.360
Now that they've lost ownership of it, 
my family is looking after it.

16:01.560 --> 16:03.570
Is that what's happened?

16:03.570 --> 16:05.110
Beautiful, isn't it?

16:05.380 --> 16:09.620
Ever since I was a child, this place 
has always been filled with flowers.

16:11.110 --> 16:14.610
Because this is where 
Frederica rests, you see.

16:18.090 --> 16:20.800
What are those dried flower crowns?

16:20.800 --> 16:24.480
Hazelita made them before 
she went to your village.

16:24.760 --> 16:26.800
The two of them often made them together,

16:26.800 --> 16:28.080
so they must hold a lot of memories for her.

16:28.580 --> 16:31.080
Every time I see a flower crown,

16:31.080 --> 16:34.000
I feel shame for not being 
able to do anything back then.

16:36.220 --> 16:39.470
Are you sure you 
weren't able to do anything?

16:39.470 --> 16:40.620
Lawren?

16:40.620 --> 16:42.140
I'm sorry.

16:42.140 --> 16:44.140
This may be rude of me,

16:44.140 --> 16:47.110
but you and your sister stayed 
by Lady Saint Frederica's side,

16:47.110 --> 16:49.480
and Miss Hazelita was suffering so much...

16:49.980 --> 16:53.200
I just can't imagine that 
you didn't feel the same way.

16:53.530 --> 16:54.740
And...

16:55.140 --> 16:58.080
Make sure you don't lose her.

16:58.410 --> 17:00.370
those words you said to me yesterday,

17:00.370 --> 17:03.920
I felt like they were those 
of someone who had taken action.

17:04.270 --> 17:08.670
The one who sent the secret report to 
the Great Lady Saint was you, wasn't it?

17:10.350 --> 17:14.170
The actions I could take back then 
were very limited, you see.

17:14.500 --> 17:16.640
I used the fact that 
I'm from a prominent family,

17:16.640 --> 17:19.120
but sending a letter 
to the Great Lady Saint,

17:19.120 --> 17:21.780
who is so hard to reach, 
was the most I could do.

17:21.780 --> 17:24.700
You haven't told Hazelita, have you?

17:24.700 --> 17:27.060
I didn't want her to brood over it too much.

17:27.610 --> 17:31.020
I tried to take Frederica 
away many times, too...

17:31.020 --> 17:32.440
but I haven't told her that either.

17:32.440 --> 17:34.960
What? "Take her away"?

17:34.960 --> 17:36.570
Were you all right after that?

17:36.570 --> 17:39.020
Yes. They were all failed attempts.

17:39.020 --> 17:41.140
The lady herself refused me, you see.

17:41.140 --> 17:44.830
Apparently, as a lady saint, 
she had a certain way she wanted to live.

17:45.160 --> 17:48.280
Even after searching through all 
the literature I could find on lady saints,

17:48.280 --> 17:51.840
I still couldn't understand 
why she felt that way.

17:52.320 --> 17:56.070
But I do know that it isn't 
that she didn't want to live.

17:56.640 --> 17:58.860
The fact that I couldn't protect her...

17:58.860 --> 18:00.730
Even now, I blame myself.

18:02.520 --> 18:03.850
Enough of that.

18:04.040 --> 18:06.930
Speaking of one's regrets 
only brings embarrassment.

18:06.930 --> 18:09.640
Since I'm speaking 
with a pastor and a lady saint,

18:09.640 --> 18:11.360
I said more than I meant to.

18:11.690 --> 18:13.480
I'll head back first.

18:13.480 --> 18:16.200
What? Mister Giselbert...

18:17.820 --> 18:19.180
You take care of the rest!

18:20.320 --> 18:21.280
Um...

18:21.720 --> 18:25.210
Lady Saint, shall we head back, too?

18:28.990 --> 18:30.720
I-I'm sorry!

18:30.720 --> 18:33.400
I don't know why. 
These tears just started falling.

18:34.840 --> 18:40.240
The two of them really cared 
about Lady Saint Frederica, didn't they?

18:41.240 --> 18:42.240
<i>Oh.</i>

18:42.840 --> 18:46.090
<i>This is what you wanted to say, isn't it?</i>

18:51.710 --> 18:52.600
Frederica!

18:52.930 --> 18:54.230
Gil!

18:54.230 --> 18:55.920
Welcome! Look!

18:55.920 --> 18:59.190
This flower crown turned out very nicely.

18:59.190 --> 19:01.240
Oh, um, yes.

19:01.240 --> 19:02.880
Didn't it?

19:04.660 --> 19:05.990
Frederica...

19:06.870 --> 19:09.410
I think we should run away 
from here after all.

19:10.310 --> 19:11.750
How lovely.

19:11.750 --> 19:13.780
It's like a story from a novel!

19:13.780 --> 19:15.230
Frederica!

19:15.590 --> 19:16.770
I can't.

19:17.200 --> 19:19.330
I'm a lady saint.

19:19.330 --> 19:22.660
If people need me, then I will be 
here to meet their needs.

19:22.660 --> 19:23.920
What are you saying?!

19:23.920 --> 19:25.040
Besides...

19:25.040 --> 19:29.680
if you did something like that you 
and your family would be in danger.

19:30.080 --> 19:33.200
You have a precious little sister.

19:33.920 --> 19:36.100
I want you to love her.

19:38.160 --> 19:39.820
<i>You...</i>

19:39.820 --> 19:42.850
<i>You only ever prayed 
for the happiness of others, didn't you?</i>

19:42.850 --> 19:44.480
Mister Giselbert!

19:45.550 --> 19:46.780
You two.

19:47.120 --> 19:51.490
Mister Giselbert, you said that
you researched lady saints, didn't you?

19:51.490 --> 19:53.420
Oh, yes.

19:53.430 --> 19:56.050
Mostly old records and folklore.

19:56.050 --> 20:00.560
Then, have you heard 
of the divine protection of lady saints?

20:00.560 --> 20:04.550
It's the lady saints' will 
to protect people, isn't it?

20:04.550 --> 20:06.550
That's right. Exactly.

20:06.550 --> 20:12.800
In the future, you and Hazelita probably 
won't be gravely injured or seriously ill.

20:12.800 --> 20:13.890
What?

20:13.890 --> 20:18.180
Lady Saint Frederica wanted 
the two of you to live and move forward.

20:18.180 --> 20:20.060
This is her divine protection.

20:20.900 --> 20:26.300
Even at the very end, 
she cared about you two very much.

20:28.640 --> 20:32.620
All this when you were 
the one dying of illness.

20:32.620 --> 20:36.200
You really did only wish 
for the happiness of others.

20:36.200 --> 20:38.000
What a troublesome person.

20:42.220 --> 20:43.830
Lady Saint?

20:44.430 --> 20:46.180
<i>These tears...</i>

20:46.550 --> 20:50.220
<i>Are they from a sense of empathy 
with the lady saint?</i>

20:51.840 --> 20:53.260
<i>Frederica...</i>

20:53.780 --> 20:59.440
<i>you knew the happiness of being 
with the person you love, too, didn't you?</i>

22:35.720 --> 22:36.760
Gil?!

22:36.760 --> 22:37.670
Hey.

22:38.920 --> 22:41.060
Th-This is the second floor, you know?

22:41.060 --> 22:42.810
My test results were poor,

22:42.810 --> 22:45.620
so my parents forbid me 
from leaving the house.

22:45.620 --> 22:48.110
If my family weren't so strict,

22:48.110 --> 22:51.380
I would have come straight 
through the front door.

22:51.380 --> 22:54.910
But it's because you 
were born to that family

22:54.910 --> 22:58.390
that you're allowed to see me, 
a lady saint, right?

22:58.390 --> 23:03.160
If you weren't a lady saint, 
it would be so much easier to talk to you.

23:03.160 --> 23:05.540
But if I weren't a lady saint,

23:05.540 --> 23:07.860
then you probably never would have met me,

23:07.860 --> 23:11.650
and we wouldn't have had these 
kinds of ordinary conversations.

23:11.650 --> 23:13.690
That would have been so sad, wouldn't it?

23:13.690 --> 23:15.280
When you say it like that...

23:15.520 --> 23:20.370
it sounds to me like you're the one 
who wants these ordinary conversations.

23:21.580 --> 23:25.490
I-If you don't feel the same, Gil, 
then I don't really need them.

23:25.490 --> 23:27.840
I do! I do feel the same!

23:27.840 --> 23:30.960
Strict families and lady saints aside,

23:30.960 --> 23:34.310
just being able to see you is enough.

23:36.510 --> 23:38.960
Yes. Isn't it?
